WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.670
The Atacama Desert runs right along
the shore of the Pacific Ocean.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.550
Endless water lies just offshore.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.270
Yet the Atacama is the
driest desert on Earth.

4
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.910
Other deserts are easier to explain.

5
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.630
Death Valley sits behind
four mountain ranges,

6
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.770
with under 5 centimetres of rain a year.

7
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.350
So how can a desert
beside an ocean be so dry?

8
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.730
Is it too hot for clouds to form?

9
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.450
In this mission, you'll
test five causes of aridity,

10
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.930
from pressure and winds
to distance from the sea.

11
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.670
Then you'll see how causes combine,
from Death Valley to the Sahara.

12
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.390
Your mission: explain how
the Atacama can be so dry,

13
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.230
right beside an ocean.
